  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering Integrated Rural Development in Greater Equatoria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cordaid aims to implement the Fostering Integrated Disaster Risk Management project in Magwi County. The project will improve livelihoods through engaging rural communities to develop and implement their Disaster Risk Management strategies in coordination with ongoing rural community development processes.

The project will adopt the following strategies.
-	strengthen planning and implementation capacities of sub-national administrative structures regarding gender-sensitive and risk-informed participatory socio-economic disaster risk management planning, 
The project objective is to strengthen community capacity in disaster risk management through a participatory Community Managed Disaster Risk Reduction approach. 
The ultimate project goal is to strengthen the planning and implementation capacities at the subnational level to implement Integrated Disaster Risk Management (DRM) measures identified in 5 bomas in Magwi County of Eastern Equatoria State
The project Fostering Integrated Disaster Risk Management FIDRM in Magwi County of Eastern Equatoria will target the rural population with a focus on agricultural households in five selected communities in Magwi County in Eastern Equatoria: 
In the first phase, the project will target Madi communities in Magwi County as follows:</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project promotes climate-smart farming techniques to achieve sustainable food security through food crops as a short-term outcome and enhance the income of supported beneficiaries from selling coffee as a medium-term outcome and promoting investment/ savings from teak as a long-term outcome. 
The project team will select at least 3 beneficiaries as authors of the articles from each of the 5 bomas. 
Beneficiaries will also be informed of their roles, project objectives, target locations, and approaches to be used among others. Communities will remain an integral part of the project and will continuously be informed of the project processes including anticipated project outcomes and results. 
Cordaid shall seek the authorization of beneficiaries before sharing information in reports, photos, and publications.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will foster rural development and disaster risk management through a 
participatory Community Managed Disaster Risk Reduction approach. The ultimate project 
goal is to strengthen the planning and implementation capacities at subnational level to
implement Integrated Rural Development and DRM measures identified to restore and 
stabilise the productive bases in the eight communities (Payam, Boma). 
The project will be implemented in Greater Equatoria targeting rural population with a 
focus on agricultural households in eight selected communities in the two counties of Yei 
and Magwi in the states of Central and Eastern Equatoria respectively:
-Yei River County County (CES): -covering Yari, Jombu (Mugwo Payam), and Ronyi (Yei 
Town Payam) 
-Magwi County (EES) the project will target cover Moli Tokuro, Opari, Kerepi (Pageri 
Payam), and Olikwi, Jelei (Madi Corridor).</narrative>
  </description>
